- PERCEPTION: searching a room or area is a move action. DC varies: 0 for obvious things, 15 for
  typical hidden objects, 20+ for well-hidden items, 25+ for secret doors. Detect traps with
  Perception (rogues only for magical traps, DC = 25+ for most).
- TAKE 10 / TAKE 20: if not in immediate danger or distracted, the character can Take 10 on skill
  checks. Taking 20 requires 20x the normal time and assumes eventual failure triggers (cannot
  Take 20 if failure has consequences like setting off a trap).
- KNOWLEDGE CHECKS: cannot be retried; a failed check means the character does not know. DC 10
  for common knowledge, DC 15 for uncommon, DC 20+ for rare, DC 25+ for obscure, DC 30+ for
  extremely obscure. Add +5 per related question beyond the first.
- DETECT MAGIC: 60 ft cone, concentration (standard action each round). Round 1: presence/absence.
  Round 2: number of auras and strongest. Round 3: location and strength of each. Spellcraft
  DC 15 + spell level to identify a school; DC 15 + caster level for an active effect.
- DISABLE DEVICE: 1 round for simple devices, 1d4 rounds for complex/tricky ones, 2d4 rounds
  for intricate. Failing by 5+ triggers the trap. Requires thieves' tools (improvised: -2).
